We switched all feedback gains to negative signs so the controller pushes opposite to deviations: a negative weight on cart position (w₀) will generate a leftward force when the cart drifts right and vice‑versa, centering the cart; a negative weight on pole angle (w₁) applies a force opposite to the lean, counter‑acting pole tilt. Negative velocity gains (w₂, w₃) damp cart and pole motion, reducing overshoot and oscillations. The bias term is kept zero to avoid any constant offset that could re‑introduce drift. This sign inversion directly addresses the systematic left/right bias observed in previous trials and should markedly extend episode length, moving us toward the target reward near 1000.
