response-og: params[0]: -1.0, params[1]: -5.0, params[2]: -1.0, params[3]: -2.0, params[4]: 0.0
These values aim to provide strong negative feedback on all four state components: a negative weight on cart position (params[0]) pushes the cart back toward the centre when it drifts right, a large negative weight on pole angle (params[1]) generates a corrective force opposite to any tilt, and negative weights on both cart velocity (params[2]) and pole angular velocity (params[3]) dampen motion. The bias term is set to zero to keep the control symmetric around the origin. This combination follows the classic LQR intuition for the inverted‑pendulum, seeking to counteract both positional and angular drift while avoiding excessive saturation, which should allow the agent to stay balanced much longer and move toward the target reward near 1000.
