response-og: params[0]: -2.0, params[1]: 7.0, params[2]: -1.0, params[3]: 3.0, params[4]: 0.5
The chosen weights follow a classic LQR‑style sign pattern: a negative cart‑position gain (w0) to pull the cart back toward the center when it drifts right, a positive pole‑angle gain (w1) to accelerate the cart in the direction of the lean (which moves the cart under the falling mass), a negative cart‑velocity gain (w2) to damp motion, and a positive pole‑angular‑velocity gain (w3) to provide predictive correction. The small positive bias term (b) offsets the remaining systematic rightward force, aiming for near‑zero net drift and thus longer stays within the ±0.2 m position tube. This combination is expected to keep the cart centered while maintaining stable pole control, increasing the episode length toward the target 1000 steps.
